@startuml esign-webhook
'==============================================================================
' Figure (Chapter IV, Electronic signature): component view of the webhook
' return path. DocuSeal reports signer progress to a verified webhook
' endpoint; status is applied idempotently to the SignatureRequest aggregate;
' on completion a reactor activates the contract and links the signed PDF
' back as a DocumentLink. A reconciliation cron self-heals missed webhooks.
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg esign-webhook.puml  then  rsvg-convert -f pdf
'==============================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ranksep 30
skinparam nodesep 24

cloud "DocuSeal\n(e-signature provider)" as ds

package "CLMPilot backend" {
  component "Webhook endpoint\n(verifies provider signature\nbefore parsing)" as hook
  component "Command bus" as cbus
  component "SignatureRequest\naggregate" as sig
  component "Signature reactor\n(contract domain)" as reactor
  component "Contract\naggregate" as contract
  component "DocumentLink\naggregate" as doclink
  component "ESignatureProvider\nadapter" as adapter
  component "Reconciliation job\n(cron)" as recon
}

ds --> hook : signer / submission\nevents (webhook)
hook --> cbus : apply-status command\n(system dispatch, idempotent)
cbus --> sig : status events
sig --> reactor : SignatureCompletedEvent
reactor --> contract : mark signed,\ndraft to active
reactor --> adapter : fetch signed PDF
adapter --> ds : download signed\ndocument
reactor --> doclink : link signed PDF\nto the contract
recon --> adapter : poll requests stuck\nin a sent state

note bottom of hook
  Routing identifiers (tenant, contract,
  request) travel in the provider's
  submission metadata.
end note
@enduml
